   "speaker": "Josh Frydenberg",
   "party": "Liberal",
   "state": "federal",
   "date": "2017-06-15",
   "stage_hint": null,
   "brief": "The Treasury Laws Amendment (GST Integrity) Bill 2017, announced by Minister Kelly O'Dwyer on 31 March 2017 and applying from 1 April 2017, requires purchasers of gold, silver and platinum supplied as taxable supplies to remit GST to the ATO via a reverse charge. The bill also clarifies that precious metals are not second-hand goods, targeting tax avoidance and fraud while securing additional funding for states and territories."
  }
